    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77710.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 26,
    "turn_text": "So first of all, power to her and the women's caucus were standing up on the floor and calling it out. How many times in the past have women been demeaned and degraded and because of power dynamics had to just take it. How many women go to jobs today and have to accept you know, harassment, because their jobs might depend on it, and their families are depending on it. How many people whose life is based on the tips they get, get somebody at some table thinking they have some right to say something to somebody? Sexual harassment has worked. So I just want to say, what was powerful to me about AOC is her standing up saying, this isn't about me, one person. This is about a man feeling entitled. to demean and degrade all women because when you use that word, in that manner, you're degrading women. And clearly he showed who he is. And I think the way she handled herself, she showed who she is.",
