    "turn_text": "So there are punishments like in the Senate, you could be something called, it's going to get technical. Now rule 19 where you could, you know, there's ethics commissions. I don't know if that will happen in the House. I don't know what will happen, but we should have standards of conduct that are enforced. And again, I also think that this is not a part is an issue. using that foul language like he did he should be held accountable period in the public in the public square regardless of what your party is but unfortunately now we live in it we live in a nation has become so hyper partisan part so hyper as part as eyes that that's a word that that um that we immediately fall into ranks behind the person of our party and don't criticize them. That's the problem with Donald Trump. I'm telling you right now, if Obama did a fraction of the things that this person did, my colleagues on the other side, that would be calling bloody murder, but because they're Trump, they're defending them. When they know there's no defense for the kind of things he's saying, you know, saying, you know, shithole countries referring to African nations, where he is demeaning and degrading entire cities and regions of our country like he did to the city of Baltimore, like he's saying, go back You know, go back to where you came from to three women of color who were born in the United States of America to three congresswomen. You know, they forgive Trump or they ignore the willful ignorance to what he's doing. We've just got to get back to the point where there's certain human decency. And then if there's violations of that, we call that out.",
