    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "Well, first and foremost, Donald Trump has a long history in New Jersey. His daughter married a famous New Jersey family that used to be Democrats. So I got to know him through them. And so I've had meetings with Donald Trump before he became President Trump. And I've had, since then, I guess one meeting in the White House on a big infrastructure project that's really important to the state of New Jersey, which, and New York, frankly, the tunnels going underneath the Hudson. We need new rail tunnels. And so I went to the White House. And so, you know, I did not bring the long list of things from the time he started his campaign, talking about Mexicans and Muslims to his Axis Hollywood tape. I didn't bring that long list to read off or call him out, but I still feel I shouldn't remain silent in what he does. But let me tell you something, I shock you. I also believe that he shouldn't drag me so low as to make me hate him. I was running for a stage in Iowa when I was running for president at the edge of the stage before I jumped up on it. There was a big guy and he stopped me. He goes, dude, I want you to punch Donald Trump in the face. And I looked him in a smile and go, man, that's a felony. I laughed with him. I go, that That's not how you beat that energy by bringing that same energy. You and I've been in situations, I'm sure, as guys growing up when we did, where somebody's got that dark energy, we bring more dark energy and it descends and brings everybody that ruins the whole mood. But if you counter that energy in the way that John Lewis did, who meant hate with love, didn't mean he sanctioned what they did, he still stood up against it. But darkness, as King said, can't drive out darkness, You know, only light can do that. Hate can't drive out hate. And what we need in this country is not all of us to be descending further into sort of hatred of each other. We need to find a way to flip the script and change the energy, change the frequency and demand that we become a nation that is really a more beloved community. And you can't make it a more beloved community by not evidencing that by being a representation of that yourself.",
