    "turn_text": "Right, again, like you said, it starts with demand at the top. I'm not, at this point, I'm not Democrat or Republican. I'm independent. So I'm looking at each side and seeing what's going on. I do agree with you. If basically Donald Trump is everything that they thought Obama would be. But he wasn't. So I agree with you on that. And I agree with you on the fact that we have to, as a country, have more light come out of this, because we are so divisive. But even down to the mass, what do you think about the mass issue and politicizing of the mass? And the Democrats are welled, and Republicans don't wear it. What are your thoughts on that?",
