  {
    "episode_id": 77710,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77710.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 33,
    "turn_text": "Well, I agree with that 100% and I do say this based on what has happened since the passing of George Floyd. We have now seen what people want. We've seen what people feel. We've seen people mobilizing the way that we haven't seen since the 1960s. So I do think that this 2020 election, if it's a landslide, to me, if it's a landslide, it's going to be either the landslide one way or the other. With that being said, I want to talk to you about Joe Biden. When, as an African-American, what was your take on Joe Biden saying, quote unquote, if you have a problem figuring out whether you're for me or Trump, you're not black. As an African-American, how did you feel about that?",
