    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77710.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 36,
    "turn_text": "Not that particular comment, but you know, look, Joe Biden was my competitor. He and I both ran for press, and I stood next to him on a stage. And there were times where he showed me, especially one moment right in the beginning of the campaign, I was on CNN talking about him. Think about this for a second. I was calling him out on CNN. I get off of CNN. It was late at night, and he calls me up. Not to get mad at me, not to yell at me, but to say, Corey, this is where my heart is. My words may have been wrong, but this is where my heart is. You know my heart. I was really impressed with that. In that moment, he started opening me up to realize what kind of person he is. calls me up coming off of TV to say, hey, I want you to hear from my heart. My words may have been wrong, but I want you to know where my heart is. And so that's why I'm saying, like, I'm out all the time. You and I both, I operate at high stakes negotiations, everything like this. That kind of a spirit is we need so much more of it in America right now. And to get it from the White House, because I'm telling you right now, I heard President Obama say things that he wishes he could take back. He wrote something really beautiful towards the end of his presidency, that when you're president, you make the smallest little misstep or mistake, or everybody sees it. But how you handle it, how you handle it? It's important. It's important. 100%.",
