    "turn_idx": 43,
    "turn_text": "Yeah. And the federal protections on evictions run out this week. So we have Republicans who are not even at the negotiating table yet, while millions and millions of Americans, you and I know this because we know folk. that unemployment insurance, it was a difference between the making rent or not, being able to feed their families or not, having to sell off their wedding ring or not. And so there's a lot we have to deal with in this COVID package. money for our schools money for state and local governments money for our hospitals monies for more testing but just that the sheer compassion and empathy that in the richest nation in the world where we unemployment went up last week we shouldn't plunge millions of americans in the financial insecurity by cutting off their uh... by allowing their unemployment insurance to end that's that's where i am right now that is really uh... just I have a heavy heart man right now. I'm hurting because I know my country has more love for itself and its people than what we're seeing right now in the decisions being made by this president and the leader of the Senate, Mitch McConnell.",
