    "turn_text": "rents. He did freeze rent. So, so look, I give our governor overall high marks. I mean, he is, because I was with him through this. Remember, New Jersey is one of the states, few states right now, whether our COVID cases are going down. But it is, it is. And it is right now it is. That doesn't mean we could, you and I could go out and party this weekend and think there's not going to be consequences to that. And we need to stay social distance. We need to keep wearing our masks. We need to keep wearing our masks. Yo, Kev, don't leave, man. Sorry about that, man. We need to keep wearing our masks, and we need to do what's right. But the governor only has certain levers. He's not the all-powerful emperor. He doesn't control federal commerce. He doesn't, you know, you say freeze card notes. I know he would want to do that, but he might get sued, dragged into court, and lose. And then I have to be honest with you, New Jersey right now, like every one of our 50 states is broke. because all those sales revenue all the um revenue from uh uh that states rely on revenues are going down and guess what he's been doing he has been spending more money helping schools with more money meeting this crisis and so my job as a senator one of the top things i have to do and by the way all fifty governors have asked for this is to get billions of dollars we bailed out And I believe we should have the airline industry to help them keep their employees, major corporations. But now we're going to put this state and our local cities. I don't know what time you live in. There's going to be massive layoffs all across America of teachers and firefighters, all kind of folks. because we don't have the governments are broke. So one of the big things I'm trying to do to help our state man is battle it out with other Democrats and some Republicans I should say against Mitch McConnell who already said he wants the state to go bankrupt to battle it out to try to get states and local